    "final_answer": "I have found all the information needed to answer the task. Based on my research using Google and the Wikipedia article on Proxima Centauri, here is the answer:\n\n## Answer\n\n**The closest star system to the Solar System is the Alpha Centauri system**, located approximately 4.25 light-years away in the constellation of Centaurus. This system consists of three stars:\n- **Alpha Centauri A** (Rigil Kentaurus)\n- **Alpha Centauri B** (Toliman)\n- **Alpha Centauri C** (Proxima Centauri) — the nearest individual star to the Sun\n\n**Discovered planets in the system:**\n\nProxima Centauri has **two confirmed exoplanets and one candidate exoplanet**:\n\n1. **Proxima Centauri b** — An Earth-sized exoplanet orbiting Proxima Centauri at a distance of about 0.05 AU (7.5 million km) with an orbital period of approximately 11.2 Earth days. It orbits within the star's habitable zone, where temperatures could allow liquid water to exist.\n\n2. **Proxima Centauri d** — A sub-Earth planet orbiting roughly 0.028 AU (4.2 million km) from the star with an orbital period of about 5.1 days.\n\n3. **Proxima Centauri c** — A disputed/candidate sub-Neptune planet orbiting at roughly 1.5 AU (220 million km) from the star.",
